    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Sometimes its nice to programatically make or modify a comment e.g. something like this:\r\n// ------------------------- my comment -------------------------\r\n\r\nCould mini.comment expose a few things (e.g. is the current line commented) as primitives to aid in hacking together something that generates a comment?\r\n\r\nI have in mind a lighter version of Comment.nvim's api module",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Sometimes its nice to programatically make or modify a comment e.g. something like this:<br>\n// ------------------------- my comment -------------------------</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Could mini.comment expose a few things (e.g. is the current line commented) as primitives to aid in hacking together something that generates a comment?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have in mind a lighter version of Comment.nvim's api module</p>",
    "bodyText": "Sometimes its nice to programatically make or modify a comment e.g. something like this:\n// ------------------------- my comment -------------------------\nCould mini.comment expose a few things (e.g. is the current line commented) as primitives to aid in hacking together something that generates a comment?\nI have in mind a lighter version of Comment.nvim's api module",
