            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "There are [`get_commentstring()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0f93724569ebf27b6b3bc7130d8044a9020a8cc5/doc/mini-comment.txt#L196) and [`toggle_lines()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0f93724569ebf27b6b3bc7130d8044a9020a8cc5/doc/mini-comment.txt#L154) functions which I think is enough for this module. Having commentstring, users can test if the line matches it (granted, with a bit of parsing beforehand) while `toggle_lines()` takes care of a proper commenting.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">There are <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0f93724569ebf27b6b3bc7130d8044a9020a8cc5/doc/mini-comment.txt#L196\"><code class=\"notranslate\">get_commentstring()</code></a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0f93724569ebf27b6b3bc7130d8044a9020a8cc5/doc/mini-comment.txt#L154\"><code class=\"notranslate\">toggle_lines()</code></a> functions which I think is enough for this module. Having commentstring, users can test if the line matches it (granted, with a bit of parsing beforehand) while <code class=\"notranslate\">toggle_lines()</code> takes care of a proper commenting.</p>",
            "bodyText": "There are get_commentstring() and toggle_lines() functions which I think is enough for this module. Having commentstring, users can test if the line matches it (granted, with a bit of parsing beforehand) while toggle_lines() takes care of a proper commenting.",
